{
  "manufacturer": "inepro Metering",
  "manufacturer_slug": "inepro-metering",
  "model": "4PU / 4PS three-phase energy meter",
  "model_slug": "4pu-4ps",
  "short_model": "4PU / 4PS",
  "aliases": [
    "4PU",
    "4PS",
    "inepro 4PU",
    "inepro 4PS"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
  "applies_to": "4PU (meter code 1111) and 4PS (1112) MID three-phase DIN-rail meters with Modbus, user manual version 1.03 (2025).",
  "summary": "The 4PU and 4PS are inepro's MID three-phase DIN-rail energy meters with RS485 Modbus RTU, M-bus and Bluetooth options. Values are IEEE 754 floats sent high word first, read with function 03 from hex blocks 4000h (setup), 5000h (live values) and 6000h (energy, four tariffs and quadrant reactive energy). This map covers per-phase voltages, currents, powers, power factor, frequency, energy counters and the writable communication, tariff, pulse and display settings.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "The map prints hex addresses that go into the request unchanged; the manual's write examples are 01 06 4003 000A (set Modbus ID) and 01 06 6048 0002 (set tariff). So 5012h (total active power) is wire address 20498."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "4PU and 4PS Series MID Three phase energy meter - User manual",
    "doc_number": "Version 1.03",
    "revision_date": "2025",
    "url": "https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/6617f74190bf0a53bfd776e8/6877702cbeaaaf598808a327_4PU%204PS%20Full%20user%20manual%20V1.03.pdf",
    "pages": "Modbus ID and combination code 7.6.6/7.6.15 (pp. 18-21); Appendix 3 Modbus A3.1 (p. 28); register map A3.2 (pp. 29-33); write commands (pp. 34-35)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The PDF is inepro's own user manual (hosted on inepro's website CDN).",
    "'Float ABCD' = IEEE 754 32-bit float, high word first; 'Signed' rows are 16-bit integers.",
    "Data type setting (4026h) offers 1 = standard or 2 = integer. The manual does not describe the integer encoding, and does not say which setting is the factory default; this map assumes 1 (standard), under which the map prints every value as Float ABCD.",
    "The quadrant reactive energy rows (6063h-6089h) print the unit kWh; they are reactive energies and are listed here in kvarh.",
    "Left out: serial number, meter code, checksums, active status word and CT ratio 400Ch (HEX), LCD cycle time and voltage/current rows 5000h/500Ah (marked 'PRO series only'), current direction (ASCII), error code 4015h (no code list), CT ratio 401Fh (two-word primary/secondary format, e.g. 9995/5) and pulse type 4022h (typed HEX in the read map, Signed in the write table).",
    "The day-counter write row prints length 1, but its example frame writes 2 registers with function 16; it is listed as a 2-register float.",
    "Power is in kW/kvar/kVA and energy in kWh/kvarh, as printed."
  ],
